Actually, let me look at the `SSML_EMPHASIS` case. `value = attrlookup(attr1, mnem_emphasis)` can return -1. Then `emphasis_to_pitch_range[-1]` reads before the static array. But again, static array.

Let me look at the `SSML_PROSODY` case. `SetProsodyParameter` is called with `attr1` from `GetSsmlAttribute`. Inside `SetProsodyParameter`:
```c
if ((value = attrlookup(attr1, mnem_tabs[param_type])) >= 0) {
    sp->parameter[param_type] = (param_stack[0].parameter[param_type] * value)/100;
} else {
    sign = attr_prosody_value(param_type, attr1, &value);
    ...
}
```

If `attrlookup` returns -1, it calls `attr_prosody_value`. Inside `attr_prosody_value`:
```c
while (iswspace(*pw)) pw++;
if (*pw == '+') {
    pw++;
    sign = 1;
}
if (*pw == '-') {
    pw++;
    sign = -1;
}
value = (double)wcstod(pw, &tail);
```

If `pw` is an empty string (from `GetSsmlAttribute` returning `empty`), then `*pw` is 0, `iswspace(0)` is false, so the while loop doesn't execute. Then `*pw` is 0, not '+' or '-'. Then `wcstod(pw, &tail)` with `pw` pointing to an empty string returns 0 and `tail == pw`. So it returns 100. That's fine.

